  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the first priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA n2000) is the simplest and most standard configuration in single-cell genomics: PCA is a well-understood linear encoder, single-profile avoids aggregation complexity, and no image modality or fusion is involved. This gives a reference accuracy against which all other RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), profile settings (multiprofile + aggregation), image-only models, and multimodal fusion strategies can be meaningfully compared. Establishing this anchor first reduces uncertainty about the fundamental performance floor and allows subsequent experiments to isolate the incremental contribution of each design choice (better encoder, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion) with 9 remaining experiments."
